Z||000005||WisconsinGT||10-26-1999||11:06 PM||||Looking at the original image of the formula, it is a darker yellow. <P>Here's a little info. on the cars and the people that owned them... The buitiful red Ferrari rebody was, in a previous life, an 88 Formula. The owner (Don Krause) still has alot of the original body panels and dash. I met Don and his wife that day in Wisconsin and we drove down together. That car got so much attention that day. It is truly a work of art. Don is a first class guy as well. Also, he is in the process of getting 300-340 pounds of foot torque out of it. <P>As we approached the meet, I saw a black fiero (SE I think) ahead. I thought great, we must be close. I kept hearing this rump, rump, rump as I was waiting at the stop sign. I thought to myself, what is making that noise? Then the black SE took off like a rocketship. So at the meet I found it. After inspecting the rocketship all my questions were answered. The picture of the V8 engine is evidence of that.<P>I was walking around looking for 88GT's I found one. And it was black like mine. A friendly guy sitting back in a chair with a cold one from gods country says, " what do you think?" I reply, "Looks like mine." Then he says, "Yeah, but does it sound like mine?" He proceeds to put his hand in his pocket and the car starts. I almost shit me pants. The engine was sucking some serious air too. The Turbo engine picture is evidence of that.<P>As I walked into the meet. The first thing I saw was that beautiful black 88GT on the back of the truck. It looked so fine. In my opinion there are two kinds of Fiero's the one like I have with the original rims. That I would feel comfortable driving into a Holiday Inn wearing gym shorts and a sweatshirt. Or there is the Fiero like the one on the flatbed truck, that I would feel comfortable driving into the Waldorf Astoria wearing a tux sporting a bottle of Dom. Anyway, the rims are Crager. The rims and tires will set you back $3,000. So I was told.<P>In 88 I purchased a new Formula. If I had to do it over again, it would be the rare yellow T-top Formula. Wait, I would buy a rare yellow GT with T-tops first then the Formula. <P>I now realize after Fierorama that I have alot of work to do on my GT. But as you can see, it gives a person alot of ideas to build on.||||reg||10
